/target
**/target
Cargo.lock.bak

# Build products. packaging/out is binaries, packages and the assembled
# repository tree -- hundreds of megabytes, all reproducible from a tag.
/packaging/out/

# Signing keys. These are the one thing here that cannot be regenerated without
# every user re-trusting a new key, so they are kept out of the repository and
# backed up out of band. See packaging/repo/README.md.
/packaging/repo/keys/

# Third-party binaries, and the installer itself. The installer no longer
# carries NSSM (it fetches it during setup), but vendor\nssm.exe is still where
# install-service.ps1 looks when run straight from the repository - put one
# there with `install-service.ps1 -Action FetchNssm -Dest vendor\nssm.exe`.
# The .exe is a build product of build-installer.ps1.
/packaging/windows/vendor/
/packaging/windows/Breeze-Core-Setup.exe
packaging/repo/portage-git/
packaging/repo/homebrew-git/
